ketch. Every door is given tag 'D' and every window tag 'W' so the software numbers them in reading order; no numbers have been invented.", "Every opening position and width was MEASURED off the drawing against the written 25'-3\" overall (about 37.1 pixels per foot on the supplied render) - not one of them is written on the sketch. Values are quoted to roughly the nearest 0.05 ft and each may be out by up to about 0.5 ft.", "I could not zoom into this render (no image tooling available in this environment), so all measured figures come from a single full-page reading. The room geometry rests on the written dimensions and is firm; the measured opening positions are the softest numbers in this file.", "The entry steps carry no dimensions. Two treads at LVL:+0'-6\" and LVL:+1'-0\" arriving at the Verandah's +1'-6\"; the 1'-0\" going and the 7'-3\" width were measured. The UP arrow points east, so the climb starts at the west - up_from 'left'. There is no wall across the west side of the Verandah for the steps to break through.", "There is NO staircase on this sketch. The only UP mark belongs to the two entry steps, which are recorded in 'steps'.", "The Verandah's north edge is drawn as two short hatched wall stubs at the NW and NE corners with a thin double line between them, and a second thin double line runs down the Verandah's east edge. The thin double lines are read as railings. Neither the stubs nor the railings are dimensioned or labelled; stubs taken as 9\", railings as 4\", and the stub lengths (1'-7\" NW, 1'-5\" NE) were measured.", "The east railing is drawn at the building's east edge. It has been placed on the east exterior wall's centre-line, x = 24.875, so the two lines align.", "The Verandah's written depth 8'-0\" is taken as the centre-line dimension from the south wall (y = 17.5) to the north railing line (y = 25.5); its clear depth then scales 7'-7 1/2\". The written 25'-10 1/2\" overall closes on the outer faces, y = 0 to y = 25.875.", "Between the Toilet's east wall (x = 8.9375) and the Bedroom's east wall (x = 13.9375) the sketch draws NO line on the Foyer's south side - the Foyer runs straight into the Bedroom across that roughly 5'-0\" span. No wall is listed there. Because the Foyer zone box must be 6'-0\" deep to match its written size, it overlaps the Bedroom zone box by 1'-0\" over that open span; that is a labelling overlap only, with nothing built on it.", "The wall dividing the Foyer/Office column from the Bedroom/Kitchen column STEPS, and has been traced as drawn: south along x = 15.5625 from the Verandah wall to y = 10.9375, west to x = 13.9375, then south along x = 13.9375 to the south wall. It has not been straightened.", "That step leaves a 1'-7 1/2\" x 3'-9 1/2\" notch of the Office lying west of the Office's written 8'-9\" x 10'-0\" rectangle (x 14.125 to 15.75, y 7.125 to 10.9375). The Office room box covers only the labelled rectangle, so that notch carries no zone label.", "A thin UNHATCHED vertical line is drawn inside the Toilet about 3'-2\" from its west wall, running the full 5'-0\" depth. It carries no label and no thickness callout, and the Toilet's only door is at the far east end - a masonry partition there would leave the west compartment with no access. It has been read as a shower or WC screen and is NOT listed as a wall. If it is in fact a partition, the Toilet needs a second door that the sketch does not draw.", "Each window has a dashed three-sided box drawn outside the wall against it, read as a sunshade/chajja. Over the Office's east window that dashed box runs about 4'-0\" further south than the bold glazing line; the window has been taken from the bold line alone (about 3'-0\"), and the extra dashed extent is unexplained.", "The Office's east window is NOT centred on the Office - as drawn it sits about 1'-7\" north of centre. The Kitchen's east window and the Bedroom's south window are drawn centred; the Toilet's west window sits hard toward the south end of that wall. All four have been placed where they are drawn, not auto-centred.", "The Toilet window is reported as a 'window' with the mark 'W', per instruction, for the software to re-mark as a ventilator.", "Door leaf widths were taken from the drawn leaves and the wall gaps, which disagree by up to 6\": Verandah-to-Foyer about 3'-5 1/2\" (recorded 3'-6\"), Office-to-Kitchen about 3'-5\" (recorded 3'-6\"). No door measures wider than 3'-6\", so all five are single doors; none is drawn with two leaves.", "The north point is a square block with 'NORTH' lettered above it. North is taken as up the sheet (north_deg 90); the block itself does not carry an arrow that settles the direction.", "The Bedroom (13'-0\" x 11'-0\") has no door of its own - it is entered through the open 5'-0\" span off the Foyer. That is what the sketch draws; no door has been added.", "The Kitchen has two doors as drawn - one from the Office at its north-west and one from the Bedroom at its south-west. Both are traced as found.", "No level is written for the Toilet, Bedroom, Office or Kitchen; only the Verandah and Foyer carry LVL:+1'-6\".", "The sketch gives only the two overall dimension strings - no intermediate dimension stations are drawn - so 'dims' carries only the overall ticks.", "No separate plot boundary is drawn. 'plot' is the building footprint, 25'-3\" x 25'-10 1/2\".", "The meaning of the letter 'C' below the bottom dimension line (section mark, grid label or sheet mark) is not shown."], "elec": [{"code": "WL", "x": 4.145833333333333, "y": 25.3, "room": "Verandah", "tag": "BAL1-L-01", "watts": 7, "height_mm": 2100, "circuit": "L1", "angle": 270, "size": 0, "controls": [], "note": "wall light on the terrace wall \u2014 open to sky, no slab for a ceiling fitting; IP65", "visible": true}, {"code": "WL", "x": 12.4375, "y": 25.3, "room": "Verandah", "tag": "BAL1-L-02", "watts": 7, "height_mm": 2100, "circuit": "L1", "angle": 270, "size": 0, "controls": [], "note": "wall light on the terrace wall \u